<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson wins 680 mln SKR Panafon order.</title>
<headline>Ericsson wins 680 mln SKR Panafon order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms giant LM Ericsson AB on Thursday said it had won a three year GSM contract worth 680 million crowns from the joint venture Panafon in Greece.  </p>
<p>Ericsson will deliver and install a complete GSM system, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Panafon is one of two Greek GSM operators, Ericsson said.</p>
<p>Panafon consists of Vodafone Group Plc, which holds 45 percent in the venture, France Telecom with holds 35 percent, local company Intracom SA with 10 percent and Databank S.A. of Greece with 10 percent, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
